  p("U1","1.3","Representing Motion","2.C","Which interval in the Motion Sensor Trial has the greatest average speed?","From 2 s to 3 s",["From 0 s to 1 s","From 1 s to 2 s","All three intervals have equal speed"],"The one-second position changes are 2 m, 4 m, and 6 m. Because the time intervals are equal, the 2-to-3 s interval has the greatest average speed.",{stimulusGroupId:"phys1-motion-table",stimulus:motionData});
  p("U1","1.2","Displacement, Velocity, and Acceleration","3.C","Which claim is best supported by the Motion Sensor Trial?","The cart accelerates to the right because its displacement per second increases.",["The cart moves at constant velocity because time intervals are equal.","The cart accelerates left because its position is positive.","The cart remains at rest because no force data are shown."],"Successive equal-time displacements grow from 2 m to 4 m to 6 m, so average velocity becomes more positive. That trend supports rightward acceleration.",{stimulusGroupId:"phys1-motion-table",stimulus:motionData});

