  p("U6","6.4","Conservation of Angular Momentum","2.B","What angular-momentum magnitude is shown in every Spinning Stool state?","6.0 kg*m^2/s",["1.5 kg*m^2/s","4.0 kg*m^2/s","12 kg*m^2/s"],"For each state L = Iω. State A gives (4.0)(1.5) = 6.0 kg·m²/s, and B, C, and D yield the same product.",{stimulusGroupId:"phys1-angular-momentum-table",stimulus:angularMomentumData});
  p("U6","6.4","Conservation of Angular Momentum","2.C","From state A to state C in the Spinning Stool Trial, how do inertia and angular speed change?","Inertia halves while angular speed doubles.",["Both inertia and angular speed halve.","Both inertia and angular speed double.","Inertia doubles while angular speed halves."],"The table changes from I = 4.0 to 2.0 kg·m² and from ω = 1.5 to 3.0 rad/s. The inverse changes keep Iω constant.",{stimulusGroupId:"phys1-angular-momentum-table",stimulus:angularMomentumData});
